<title>GERMANY: Kohl says goal of halving unemployment difficult.</title>
<headline>Kohl says goal of halving unemployment difficult.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl said on Thursday the German government's goal of halving unemployment by the year 2000 was still possible but it would be difficult to achieve.</p>
<p>&quot;Fighting unemployment remains the most important domestic policy challenge,&quot; Kohl told a news conference. &quot;Current levels of above 4.1 million jobless are completely unacceptable.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
